---
description: ObjectId fields use a top-level alias and a mongoose model ref
globs: backend/src/models/**/*.js,backend/src/platform/data/baseSchema.js
alwaysApply: false
---

# Mongoose ObjectId fields

Declare `ObjectId` once at the top of each schema file. Never write
`mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId` (or `Schema.Types.ObjectId`) on field
definitions.

Every ObjectId field that points at a domain document **must** set `ref` to
the registered Mongoose model name (`User`, `Project`, `Organization`, …).

Omit `ref` only when the value is not a Mongoose document (GridFS file id)
or is polymorphic with no single model (`resourceId` on idempotency records).
Use `refPath` when a sibling field names the target model.

```js
const ObjectId = mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId;

// ❌ BAD
projectId: { type: mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId, required: true },

// ✅ GOOD
projectId: { type: ObjectId, ref: 'Project', required: true },
createdBy: { type: ObjectId, ref: 'User', default: null },
roleIds: { type: [ObjectId], ref: 'Role', required: true },
```
